<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $27.54 bln on May 16.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $27.54 bln on May 16.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $27.54 billion on May 16 from $27.29 billon a week ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  May 16	May 9	  May 17</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     23,570	23,321	 17,076</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,966	 3,966	  4,520</p>
<p>    SDRs				     3	    --	     26</p>
<p>    Total			     27,539	27,287	 21,622</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
